  "interpretation": {
    "main_signal": "On this less-templated paraphrase diagnostic, the cheap Gemma direct and worker paths outperform both direct Gemini and a Gemini-generated lexical-operator proxy on exact counts. The strong-model methods have high evidence recall but overcount semantically adjacent distractors.",
    "claim_boundary": "This is not an official RLM comparison. It supports the paper's mechanism boundary: for semantic matching, preprocessing should be a semantic worker/retriever rather than only a generated lexical operator."
  }
